    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'rule' (noun) has multiple core meanings, including 'a regulation or principle governing conduct or procedure' (e.g., 'rules of the game') and 'the exercise of authority or control; government' (e.g., 'under colonial rule'). The Japanese expression '支配' (shihai) primarily translates to 'rule' in the sense of 'domination' or 'control/governance.' It does not cover the common meaning of 'rule' as a 'regulation' or 'principle,' which is a very frequent usage in general and daily life contexts. Therefore, '支配' is semantically narrower than the general English lemma and would be unnatural or incorrect for a learner encountering 'rule' in the sense of a regulation.",
