      "surface": "規則",
      "reading": "きそく",
      "reason": "規則 (kisoku) is a more appropriate and general translation for 'rule' in the sense of 'regulation' or 'principle,' which is a core meaning of the English lemma, especially in general and daily life contexts. It better covers the common usage of 'rule' for learners. Alternatively, the loanword ルール (rūru) could also be considered for the 'regulation' sense."
